<entry dateCreated="2019-05-25T15:36:02Z" dateModified="2025-11-12T14:57:24Z" id="ãmana_c929379d-375c-438e-a9b2-54c550aed74b" guid="c929379d-375c-438e-a9b2-54c550aed74b">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>aamána</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>The bound morpheme here is /-mán/ which means 'be' or 'become'. The word in the context of 'being able' always takes Pronominal and Inflectional affixes. In the Future forms, the consonant 'm' is dropped. </text></form>
</note>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>aːmʌna</text></form>
</field>
<trait name="Past Participle" value="Past Participial"/>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>آمناࣷ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Possessed">
<form lang="bsk"><text>man</text></form>
</field>
<trait name="Possessors" value="O-Obligatorily Possessors"/>
<sense id="d6e21ecd-d7f7-451b-9245-09cc8acfad7a">
<grammatical-info value="Verb">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>1SG was able to, I was capable of</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>میں کر سکا</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ja aamána ka, gute doro ka ećam</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>If I am able to do, I will do this work as well. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ne hir doro eća, eemáni bee. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>That man was not able to do the work. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>un kheen ulle doro eća goomayuma (goo-ma-yum). </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>You will be able to do the work in time. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2021-03-12T16:16:21Z" dateModified="2025-11-12T15:23:33Z" id="aan_de44633b-cccf-4ecf-8f87-99ca5e317f88" guid="de44633b-cccf-4ecf-8f87-99ca5e317f88">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>aan</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>
Phonological Note: Ellision and Assimilation - In rapid or casual speech, aan may surface as aam due to nasal assimilation: - /n/ → /m/ before bilabial consonants like /b/ 

Example: aan bai → aam bai (Show me where is he?) This is a surface-level phonological change, not a separate lexical item. The underlying form remains aan. This is attested by the fact that aan has its prevalent Inflectional forms such as aanum (where from), aane (where at) and aana (where to) and aam does not have such forms. See more detail under /aam/.</text></form>
</note>
<relation type="Compare" ref="aam_068310a7-7fd7-49c6-818f-4577555e3d19"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="ané_603b58a8-cfac-48a2-9e49-c30afb6ac72c"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="anüm_1a1b36ad-7886-4ec3-a4bc-a15bdb8ebc90"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="ána1_21518ec8-5900-4586-8385-60055c316ea0"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>aːn</text></form>
</field>
<trait name="Noun Class" value="duwa"/>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>آن</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="da1b5ed5-d128-4e8c-b741-e3087679101f">
<grammatical-info value="Adverb">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>where, somewhere</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>کہاں</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>chell aan duwa?</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>(show me) Where is the water?</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<translation type="Free translation">
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ne hir aan bai. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>(Show me) Where is the man?</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-10-03T14:27:05Z" dateModified="2025-11-12T15:29:16Z" id="-aas1_627649e6-421c-4d05-964e-fb055f0e9f0a" guid="627649e6-421c-4d05-964e-fb055f0e9f0a">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>-aas</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="suffix"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text><span lang="bsk">The –aas suffix shifts the imperative from a direct command to a modal or circumstantial necessity—what ought to be done, needs to be said, or is due.

Syntax: [Verb stem] + –aas + Auxiliary</span></text></form>
</note>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>-aːs</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>اس</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="05994542-07d4-45b3-b151-88020a4a4521">
<gloss lang="en"><text>Verbal suffix attaches to imperative verb stems to form constructions that express necessity, obligation, or due action.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>جس کا کرنا یا ہونا با قی ہو</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>gute doro etaas duwa</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>This work needs to be done.</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ne díya ka, neġa senas duwa.</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>When he comes, he needs to be told.</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2021-01-16T03:16:36Z" dateModified="2025-11-12T15:53:00Z" id="-aas2_522dc022-42e0-4736-9953-0750b26d23a3" guid="522dc022-42e0-4736-9953-0750b26d23a3">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>-aas</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="suffix"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>-aːs</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>آس</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="ed1e5e65-083c-4c26-92c9-7baa42be77bb" order="0">
<gloss lang="en"><text>Agentive suffix, Human Actor, Someone who performs an action. </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>وہ جو کرتا ہے، فاعل  </text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>girataas hir</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>A man who performs the dance.</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ġareas hir</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>A man who talks too much.</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>mo girminaas gus men bú.</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Who is that writer woman?</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
<sense id="e768d8df-30ef-4ab3-ba69-6225fc96b98b" order="1">
<gloss lang="en"><text>Action-Based Identifier (Known for an Act, Something or someone known for an action or behavior.  </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>وہ جو کسی کام کے لیے جانا جاتا ہو۔</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>prán dellaas</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>an explosive (thing)</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>phuulʰtas</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>a blowing thing (balloon)</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>khene pilili cum ka eemallas hir bai. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>This over here is a man who would be scared, even of an ant. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
<sense id="786ce435-b9b5-44ce-bba9-d6cf7357d078" order="2">
<gloss lang="en"><text>A tool or machine by which something is done. Something that performs an action. </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>وہ چیز جو کچھ کام کرتا ہے یا جس سے کام لیا جاتا ہے۔ </text></gloss>
<example>
<translation type="Free translation">
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>an explosive, something that explodes</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-04-27T14:44:46Z" dateModified="2025-11-12T15:57:01Z" id="aaser_31154c2a-b647-4887-9cd5-a2cf20bf15f8" guid="31154c2a-b647-4887-9cd5-a2cf20bf15f8">
