<entry dateCreated="2019-05-26T14:24:11Z" dateModified="2025-11-12T16:21:27Z" id="aaṣki_1afe49f7-4611-4356-8f11-88d6ce398e8a" guid="1afe49f7-4611-4356-8f11-88d6ce398e8a">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>aaṣki</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>The word has three morphemes: aa (1SG), ..s- (bound morpheme for neck) and ki (b). This compound construction reflects inalienable possession and locative orientation, often used in contexts involving sleep, rest, or proximity to the neck. </text></form>
</note>
<relation type="Compare" ref="auṣki_09d97063-61bc-4c0f-b916-3b2e2cfd052a"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>aːʂki</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>آݜکیࣷ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Possessed">
<form lang="bsk"><text>ṣki</text></form>
</field>
<trait name="Possessors" value="U-Obligatorily Possessors"/>
<sense id="36eb2498-0a63-42f2-bfee-b29534820187">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>by my pillow side, by my bed-head. At the side of my head when lying down</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>سوتے ہوے سر کی جانب، سر ہانے کی جانب</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ja thuwek aaṣki nóos gućhayam bám</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>I was sleeping while keeping the gun by my  pillow side. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>guren guuṣki (guu-ṣ-ki) net gućha,. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Sleep while putting your hand under neck (like a pillow)</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2024-11-27T03:06:20Z" dateModified="2025-11-12T16:24:50Z" id="aat_300dd5f8-5f2f-4535-b8ce-aca4584f00ef" guid="300dd5f8-5f2f-4535-b8ce-aca4584f00ef">
