<entry dateCreated="2022-04-26T13:56:41Z" dateModified="2025-11-13T02:08:45Z" id="aidohón_6f4bf737-0caf-4092-b3cc-5cc6a988337c" guid="6f4bf737-0caf-4092-b3cc-5cc6a988337c">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>aidohón</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>Atohon is a reduced or alternate form aidohon. This variation reflects a productive alternation between /d/ and /t/ in Burushaski, especially when preceded by the negative prefix /a/. The shift may be influenced by ease of articulation, dialectal preference, or speech register.</text></form>
</note>
<relation type="Compare" ref="atohón_a0be10af-63dd-43d3-882f-556d16cce7c0"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>aidohɔn</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>ائی دوࣷہُوࣷن</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="c55110fc-d7e6-4d24-91a4-39b39987cc73" order="0">
<grammatical-info value="Prohibitive">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>Do not hold, Do not touch.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>مت پکڑو،مت چھیڑو</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ne ren ce ai dohón</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Do not hold (with) his hand. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
<sense id="57cfa098-6540-4aa1-a8dd-270f9f0a61b0" order="1">
<grammatical-info value="Prohibitive">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>Do not scuffle. Do not mess up with.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>مت چھیڑو. مت لڑو</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ne ce aidohon. ne gadero bai, gudećemi. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Do not mess with him. He is crazy, he will hit you. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-05-17T16:24:24Z" dateModified="2025-11-13T02:10:01Z" id="aiduhakinum_139d45ba-2ca8-49f5-80fa-62a05d20951f" guid="139d45ba-2ca8-49f5-80fa-62a05d20951f">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>aiduhakinum</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>The word is also observed in usage as /atohakinum/, a change of consonant /d/ to /t/.  duhakinum means learned or trained or well brought up, and /ai/ is used as a negative prefix. </text></form>
</note>
<relation type="Compare" ref="ai/-_f78b33b8-dc4e-4c15-bb91-eb5f2121dffe"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>aiduhakinum</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>ائی دُہَکِنُم</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="a0578d79-3bbd-4ea3-9153-38b59055b1ad">
<grammatical-info value="Adjective">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>(of an upbringing) ill-mannered, not brought up properly</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>غیز مہذب، بد تمیز، وہ جس کو سکھائی نہ گئی ہو۔ </text></gloss>
<example>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2022-12-05T18:15:36Z" dateModified="2025-11-13T02:11:19Z" id="aiduus_f0be512b-b49b-4a62-b7f9-18fde25d30fd" guid="f0be512b-b49b-4a62-b7f9-18fde25d30fd">
