</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>3SG.hf did not become/get</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>(انسان، مونث) نہ ہو یا بن سکی</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>mo gus paṭak amumanú.</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>That lady did not get moved.</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>mo gus lahaz amumanú. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>The lady did not become sick. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ja thát ho amumanú?</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>My grandma did not get cold, did she?</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-09-02T18:42:46Z" dateModified="2025-11-19T15:23:56Z" id="amutuk_2ad311df-ed95-4103-b4dd-c990b30346cf" guid="2ad311df-ed95-4103-b4dd-c990b30346cf">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>amutuk</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>- a-: Proximal temporal determiner prefix, indicating immediacy or nearness in time or space. 

- Often omitted in casual or rapid speech. - In some variants (e.g. Hunza), the prefix is dropped entirely, and the root muu is used instead.

 - mutuk: Root adverb meaning “now” or “at this moment.”</text></form>
</note>
<relation type="Compare" ref="mutuk_8c9f6f60-c49d-4000-b8d6-de3dd9d96f76"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>amutuk</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>امُتُک</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="ed993f3b-49d9-4541-ba77-e01f75d676c3">
<grammatical-info value="Adverb">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>now, right now</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>ابھی</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>amutuk ja apaći kheen api. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Right now I do not have time. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-03-28T05:19:32Z" dateModified="2025-11-19T15:31:09Z" id="an_f40eb149-6cfa-46ea-821a-3e6402c2237e" guid="f40eb149-6cfa-46ea-821a-3e6402c2237e">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>án</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>When used with nouns, it signifies lack of specific information about the noun. When information becomes available about the noun, then the Distal Demonstratives "se, te" are used. For example: "se buś" instead of "buś án", "te dunes" instead of "duneś án"</text></form>
</note>
<relation type="Compare" ref="han_a70b5b13-dd7b-4720-b6d0-5f5861a850d1"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="en_4ecc97bf-8f9f-496a-8b96-a15276180806"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="ek_808ff1ff-bb11-44d8-bce1-3cc0d8100d0f"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="matalán_43cdff54-5304-4f57-9d8c-956781fd849d"/>
<pronunciation>
</pronunciation>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>ʌn</text></form>
</field>
<trait name="Noun Class" value="duwa"/>
<trait name="Noun Class" value="Bi "/>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>اَن </text></form>
</field>
<sense id="d3d4acb7-0aaf-41c8-975e-6870867a42bc">
<grammatical-info value="Indefinite article">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>a (thing),  an (animal). With the meaning of 'some' it is used as an Indefinite with X-class and Y-class of Burushaski nouns as well as their corresponding adjectives.</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>śuwa buś án</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>A good cat or some good cat.</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>duneś án</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>A thought or some sort of thought</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>guse buś śuwa án bi</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>This cat is a good one.</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>buś matúm án bi. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>The cat is of some black color. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2021-06-28T06:36:15Z" dateModified="2025-11-20T04:27:37Z" id="án1_a59670c2-1469-4102-a37b-3d94ee09d132" guid="a59670c2-1469-4102-a37b-3d94ee09d132">
