<entry dateCreated="2021-01-16T02:51:37Z" dateModified="2025-11-22T16:43:53Z" id="aqáres_b9773273-c0c8-4342-88d4-0b4dd1a7a9af" guid="b9773273-c0c8-4342-88d4-0b4dd1a7a9af">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>aqáres</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>A devoiced form,  aqares ← aġares ← aiġares. The word has agrarian root, mostly used with  'channeling water through grooves and furrows. (chell eeġares). 

To refuse someone’s statement or advice is to step out of their groove or channel—not allowing yourself to be streamlined into their intended flow of thought or action.</text></form>
</note>
<relation type="Compare" ref="ġaris_ab417d38-0bf1-496c-a0af-c22b72371f50"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>aqʌrɛs</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>اقَریࣷس</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="5a7f7d10-ae3c-4365-9da7-360b93ace4f8">
<grammatical-info value="Prohibitive">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>decline, do not agree, refuse</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>انکار کرو، رضامندی ظاہر نہ کرو، نہ بولو</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>un ne bára aqares.</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>You do not agree to his statement. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
