<entry dateCreated="2021-03-31T17:17:53Z" dateModified="2025-11-22T21:47:31Z" id="arzahim_73a13cdb-a40d-483e-b605-5f5e9b66d40d" guid="73a13cdb-a40d-483e-b605-5f5e9b66d40d">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>arzahim</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="dohomor_26f94950-acf9-46ec-ba92-38cd139c92d4"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>arzahim</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>ارزَہم </text></form>
</field>
<field type="Plural Suffix">
<form lang="bsk"><text>iṅ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="334005be-5056-4b07-ae5b-dbccaab3c8e6">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>In Yasin, Arzahim is a shamanic practice of conjuring and freeing affected persons from a state of trance caused by spirits. A shaman, called bitan, interacts with the spirits or fairies through rituals and practices — claiming to neutralize their effect on human. Bitans are invited to the house of an affected person for an early night ritual, called Arzahim.  It is believed that the fairies, made upset by the bitan during Arzahim, harm other members of the community. Neighbors are notified of the schedule of the Arzahim so that they can stay inside their houses on that night. With the arrival of Islam, bitans have been replaced by other religious healers — also claiming to have knowledge of the spirits.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>ایک عمل جس میں پریوں کے یا جن بھوت کے اثر  کو ختم کرنے کے لیے کیا جاتا ہے۔ یہ عمل شام کے بعد کیا جاتا ہے اور اس کے ماہر کو بیٹن کہا جاتا ہے۔ اسلام کے بعد بروشو معاشرت میں اب مولوی یا خلیفہ بھی یہ کام کرتا ہے۔ جس رات یہ عمل ہوتا ہے اس رات ہمسایوں کو  ہدایت کی جاتی ہے کہ وہ شام کے بعد باہر نہ نکلنے ۔  </text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
