<note>
<form lang="en"><text>baat ← baad</text></form>
</note>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>baːt</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>بات</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="25f9a0ae-8880-405f-afa8-234fb71a6ad9">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>An ancient deadly tumorous disease that is considered incurable so much so that it is used as a curse word.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>ایک قدیم  جان لیوا بیماری جو بد دعائی کلمہ کے طور پر استعمال ہوتا ہے۔   </text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ne xaći baat duusum duwa? bariṅ ayećum bai.</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Does he has some sort of tumorous disease in his mouth, he is not talking. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<trait name ="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.2 Disease"/>
</sense>
</entry>
