<entry dateCreated="2019-12-25T17:11:21Z" dateModified="2025-12-03T04:32:48Z" id="baśaar-hawaall_b809502d-68be-4f3e-9be3-d74e51ad3219" guid="b809502d-68be-4f3e-9be3-d74e51ad3219">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>baśaar-hawaall</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>This is a compound of baśaar (inquiring) of Khowar and ahwal (accounts, conditions) of Urdu</text></form>
</note>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>baʃaːr-hawaːɫ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>بشر حَوال </text></form>
</field>
<sense id="11e70961-cbb6-4a9f-969a-69ee3159c253">
<grammatical-info value="Verb Phrases">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>exchange of greetings</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>حال چال پوچھنے کا عمل</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ne hir ja ayanji dii jaġa baśarhawal eti, magám llell ayeta.</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>That man came across to me, exchanged greetings, but I did not recognize him. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2023-11-14T01:59:56Z" dateModified="2025-12-03T04:36:05Z" id="baśale kutu_3bbd95f3-00e0-4b40-a53e-efb486a855fd" guid="3bbd95f3-00e0-4b40-a53e-efb486a855fd">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>baśale kutu</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="phrase"/>
<trait name="do-not-publish-in" value="Idioms"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>baʃalɛ kutu</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>بشلےࣷ کُٹُوࣷ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="cef3f4a4-0fa3-4c74-b738-8e12918a10e5">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>A seclusion room for woman at the time of birth. Though baśale kutu existed in Darʰkut and Huyeélʰti until 19th century, the custom of menstruation and birth seclusion now exists only in the words of raconteurs.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>زچگی کے وقت عورت کے لیے مخصوص علیحدگی کا کمرہ۔ بشلے کُٹُو درکوت اور ہوئیلھتی میں انیسویں صدی تک موجود رہا، مگر حیض اور پیدائش کے موقع پر علیحدگی کی یہ رسم اب صرف قصہ گوؤں کے الفاظ میں باقی ہے۔</text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2020-08-08T00:28:41Z" dateModified="2025-12-03T04:37:11Z" id="baśgálian_bb8d58e5-e56f-49d3-9cce-11c1eea50104" guid="bb8d58e5-e56f-49d3-9cce-11c1eea50104">
