<form lang="bsk"><text>baʃgʌlian</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>بَش گَلیان</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="26e1d3bc-c79d-49ae-a31a-52d70df5f4bb">
<grammatical-info value="Adjective">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>a type of of wheat crop introduced by people of Bashgal in Chitral. </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>گند م کی ایک قسم جو کہ بشگال (چترال) کے لوگوں نے یاسین میں متعارف کرایا۔ </text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2022-11-16T04:01:55Z" dateModified="2025-12-03T04:38:23Z" id="baśgili_b8be37fb-4e60-4722-9026-11375418aa14" guid="b8be37fb-4e60-4722-9026-11375418aa14">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>baśgili</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>baʃgili</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>بَش گیلیࣷ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="ebeed06e-4aae-4f6c-8001-280add00d3b8">
<gloss lang="en"><text>A square base inserted into a carved groove of a cylindric timber is called /baśgili/. This is mostly used in making wooden pots.</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>barġondokiṣe baśgili. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>The inserted base of the yeast pot. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
