<entry dateCreated="2025-12-03T17:04:00Z" dateModified="2025-12-03T17:47:02Z" id="baṭakuśi_8ed36744-c069-4882-8e48-faae06d496d9" guid="8ed36744-c069-4882-8e48-faae06d496d9">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>baṭakuśi</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>The word is a metaphoric location, a temporal schema that contains nothingness, a perception of the concrete idea of a roofless building. Burushaski is full of metaphoric locatives marked by suffixes such as -i,-ći,-kuśi etc. Read Cognitive Theory of Metaphor (CTM) to understand this phenomenon in the Burushaski language. </text></form>
</note>
<trait name="do-not-publish-in" value="Idioms"/>
<sense id="873f5c39-0b85-4c05-8569-548e56978cbd">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>in the period of nothingness, extreme poverty, times of destitute</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>کسم پُرسی کی حالت</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>go nani tati baṭakuśi um dukuusen. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Your parents got you out of destitute. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
