<entry dateCreated="2019-09-08T01:39:53Z" dateModified="2025-12-20T15:17:47Z" id="bisarʰk_2e3cf8cf-3831-47a2-9705-c53527484eeb" guid="2e3cf8cf-3831-47a2-9705-c53527484eeb">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>bisarʰk</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>
- The underlying stem contains /k/.
 - When the verb is inflected for Progressive or Future, the /k/ is systematically deleted, resulting in a smoother consonant cluster and a lighter syllable onset. 
- This deletion appears to be morphologically conditioned, not phonotactically triggered by the following segment.

/k/ → ∅ / _ {Prog, Fut}
</text></form>
</note>
<relation type="Compare" ref="táq2_ddf3208e-bcda-4042-8a3e-a6c8dd5dcec6"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="nupisarʰk_9e708014-df36-44a9-804f-0a25d7e99c69"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="bisaŝhk_93a78321-996f-4bfc-b3fb-46f96cbb2bda"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>bisar̥k</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>بسارْک</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="6d2bfb50-240e-47d4-b7ff-f263e5912dff">
<grammatical-info value="Imperative">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>cut (the crop,grass etc)</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>گندم یا گھاس کاٹ لو</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ses dowaqall iṣqá oóbisarʰk. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Get the grass cut by the people. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ja mo gus domowaqall iṣqa moóbisarʰćam. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>I will get the woman cut the grass. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
