<entry dateCreated="2019-10-24T15:34:27Z" dateModified="2025-12-15T03:41:35Z" id="bóll_05180413-1313-45ec-9fb0-bd8ffbe2217c" guid="05180413-1313-45ec-9fb0-bd8ffbe2217c">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>bóll</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="yarďoyo_ad97f76b-41ba-4f67-9e5e-42ad9ae041d6"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="bolldoin_5d4d5eb4-b42f-4499-95ce-e05f81d24d2d"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="waacukun_feed94bd-b081-46ed-aef6-ef9992314c52"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="hoļ1_0061a149-48b4-458b-afec-6639ae9cb92e"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>bɔɫ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>بوࣷلٚ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="e06acd14-669d-48a4-8264-814849e08763">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>Second line of defense, a force within a force. Junior force. With the arrival of British raj, this line of force was assigned the work of infrastructure i.e.  to build roads, bridges, forts and water channels. Members of this force are known as 'bolldoyu'</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>فوج کی ایک قسم جس کے زمہ مواصلات اور تعمرات کا کام ہوتا تھا۔ </text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-10-24T15:39:48Z" dateModified="2025-12-15T03:39:44Z" id="bolldoin_5d4d5eb4-b42f-4499-95ce-e05f81d24d2d" guid="5d4d5eb4-b42f-4499-95ce-e05f81d24d2d">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>bolldoin</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
