<entry dateCreated="2019-09-01T16:37:54Z" dateModified="2025-12-19T01:07:26Z" id="boorbór_7c5af878-92ab-4e7e-b5e9-2d6fd7208bda" guid="7c5af878-92ab-4e7e-b5e9-2d6fd7208bda">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>boorbór</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="hamaaṅgi_f6e1ce87-1aad-41cc-b7b2-aa78f6b454f0"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>boːrbɔr</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>بووࣷر بوࣷر</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="a152029f-0f81-4143-a51b-4c2ad7cf0d81">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>A traditional wedding song which is sung at the time of a girl's departure from her parent's house. A girl's departure after marriage is a tough time for parents as well as for the bride and the ritual of boorbór is an effort to admire, comfort and encourage the bride.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>لڑکی کی  رخصتی کے وقت گایا جانے والا  مخصوص گانا۔</text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
