</field>
<sense id="c3b872eb-97f1-4cc0-b7f0-a1d602bde7ca">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>At the rite in a deceased's house on the 3rd day of death, specific food is cooked, neighbors and relatives visit, prayers are offered and rituals are performed. Burusho men of letters maintain that the root word for buiki is boin, boyo(plural), a metaphysical being, boiki is the food that is cooked in the name of boin (boyo)</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>مر حوم کے گھر تیسرے  دن کی رسومات اُور ضیافت</text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
