<entry dateCreated="2019-09-22T18:28:14Z" dateModified="2025-12-13T16:29:51Z" id="bulláll_8f0f75ef-9085-48ec-8f51-d92758e8a6fb" guid="8f0f75ef-9085-48ec-8f51-d92758e8a6fb">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>bulláll</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>buɫʌɫ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>بُڵَڵ</text></form>
</field>
<trait name="Review 1" value="202512131"/>
<sense id="374a5f71-2167-451c-a80c-66e8962cd809">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>When thrashing, by employing animals, there comes a stage where animals are sent on break and the half trampled chaff or crop are let in the sun to dry off. Periodically the stalks are flipped and mixed to let the sun evenly dry the stalk. The thrashed stalk, chaff and grain all together until the winnowing stage is called /bulláll/</text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-12-27T17:31:39Z" dateModified="2025-12-13T16:27:46Z" id="bullani2_e7b64f40-3915-4cf3-b185-ff986bcd03a4" guid="e7b64f40-3915-4cf3-b185-ff986bcd03a4">
