<entry dateCreated="2019-04-05T06:48:53Z" dateModified="2025-12-24T04:56:02Z" id="chhapook_2524997a-b1a5-479a-88fe-1d92bdf227c7" guid="2524997a-b1a5-479a-88fe-1d92bdf227c7">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>chapuk</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>tshapuk</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>ڎھپُک</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Plural Suffix">
<form lang="bsk"><text>iṅ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="1a3c74cd-d2f4-4e75-ac57-5964990af040">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>A pre‑modern form of hacky sack, traditionally played with a small, torn piece of cloth kept aloft using only the feet. The number of consecutive kicks is counted, and skill is measured by control and endurance. This simple cloth‑juggling game is considered one of the oldest recreational sports in Burusho society.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text> پیاندک، ایک پھٹا ہو اکپڑا جس کو پا وٰں سے اچھال کر گنتے ہیں ۔ یہ ایک قسم کا کھیل ہے۔ </text></gloss>
<trait name ="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.6.2 Sports"/>
</sense>
</entry>
