<entry dateCreated="2022-11-11T00:28:18Z" dateModified="2026-01-01T19:38:33Z" id="ćhaća_ab652fa6-6353-42ef-8818-7e26bc00ef8b" guid="ab652fa6-6353-42ef-8818-7e26bc00ef8b">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ćhaća</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>tʃʰatʃa</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>چھچاࣷ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Plural Suffix">
<form lang="bsk"><text>miṅ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="060e11fc-5cba-4a38-988e-8b602fd7f8f1">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>an inauguration rite where a person will chant /ćhaća ćhaća/, along with prayers for speedy completion of the work or the project.  </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>دعائیہ کلمات پر مشتمل رسم جو کام کی جلدی تکمیل کے لیے ادا کی جاتی ہے۔   </text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>wawe momes dewaqall ćhaća etu, te yaṭe gaya ġa dohon. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>The granny made her grandson do the ćhaća, then she started spinning. (wool)</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2022-11-11T00:55:19Z" dateModified="2026-01-01T19:39:50Z" id="ćhaćaki_940daaac-ca30-4fda-8cdf-59cdc83e59e8" guid="940daaac-ca30-4fda-8cdf-59cdc83e59e8">
