<relation type="Compare" ref="sumbá_088d7e38-726b-4d42-b432-05d6951401ea"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="jabál_f3295798-1689-4d1a-99d2-66ca72a4e0f2"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>tʃʰani</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>چَھنیࣷ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Plural Suffix">
<form lang="bsk"><text>mo</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="ff1152b9-b14d-46d1-8d56-a92b00ba931e">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>hard‑rock chisel, iron boring bar. 
A heavy iron tool used for making holes in rock or stone for blasting. The hole is formed by repeatedly hammering the ćhani into the surface. In recent years, this traditional method has largely been replaced by hand‑held drilling machines.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>لوہے کا سلاخ جس سے پتھر وں میں سوراخ کر کے دھما کہ خیز مواد سے پتھر کو توڑ دیا جاتا ہے۔  </text></gloss>
<trait name ="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.7 Tool"/>
</sense>
</entry>
