<entry dateCreated="2020-08-15T21:31:51Z" dateModified="2026-01-02T16:29:32Z" id="ćharbát_882bd83f-941c-4e4b-be8f-f7b18ff819ba" guid="882bd83f-941c-4e4b-be8f-f7b18ff819ba">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ćharbát</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="ćher_3a764491-b84e-4be6-a420-38db3cba215d"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="bát1_bba360da-3f45-4a35-a56c-1f0f36e25333"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>tʃʰarbʌt</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>چھیࣷر بت</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Plural Suffix">
<form lang="bsk"><text>iṅ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="fa5e3b44-a89f-424d-882a-42cf789e8b18">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>A traditional wheat porridge cooked in butter, ćharbat is made from coarsely ground flour. Over time, the word has been phonologically changed and is now often mispronounced as śarbat (sorbet). The original form, however, comes from the combination of two Burushaski roots: /ćher/ and /bat/.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>ایک قسم کا تعام یا کھانا</text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2021-07-01T18:01:13Z" dateModified="2026-01-02T16:33:05Z" id="ćharbo_c11fe03d-7692-4ead-a105-a4f460338a60" guid="c11fe03d-7692-4ead-a105-a4f460338a60">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ćharbo</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>tʃʰarbo</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>چَھربوࣷ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Plural Suffix">
<form lang="bsk"><text>tiṅ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="988b66ba-3d09-485b-864e-afbb2e96fb47" order="0">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>Historically an official in the royal court or at a regional fort whose responsibilities included but not limited to carrying information, messages, announcements and orders to and from the subjects or community. </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>ایک تاریخی درباری عہدہ جس کے ذمے اطلاعات و نشریات کا کام ہوتا تھا۔ </text></gloss>
<trait name ="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.5.5.1 Title, name of honor"/>
</sense>
<sense id="04027674-51c9-4c3c-b209-bc41af222687" order="1">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>an announcer, the one who calls for something. </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>مؤذن ، اعلان کرنے والا </text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
