<entry dateCreated="2021-03-29T02:18:53Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="dardu-palaṣ_b9cd12c1-ab25-462c-bcf9-85977c5d7a8e" guid="b9cd12c1-ab25-462c-bcf9-85977c5d7a8e">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>dardu-palaṣ</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>It is quite possible that the word dardu-palaś is a corrupted pronunciation of  Dard-u-Kalaṣ, which means the Dards and the Kalash people. </text></form>
</note>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>dardu-palaʂ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>دردُ پَلش</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Plural Suffix">
<form lang="bsk"><text>iśu</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="a28cd7d8-b710-4561-a90e-dc658d728fb0" order="0">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>This term is used by Burushos of Yasin for people of mixed, unknown races primarily, the immigrant Dards.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>داردِستان کے دارد لوگوں یا متفرق مہاجر لوگوں کو بروشو دارد و پلݜ کہتے ہیں۔ </text></gloss>
</sense>
<sense id="90d18985-b7d4-4c3f-8917-3fe1b1e238de" order="1">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>In Khowar, dardu-palaś is used for miscellaneous things for which specific names are not known. </text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-04-24T14:38:48Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="dareén_5310b091-e4d1-4e14-94e1-f47f6a211d44" guid="5310b091-e4d1-4e14-94e1-f47f6a211d44">
