<form lang="bsk"><text>dintshɛrum pʰaiŋ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>دن ڎھیࣷرُم پھئنٚ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="f4dc8a50-8db7-4be5-904f-185520949571" order="0">
<grammatical-info value="Adjective">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>expanded lie</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>جھوٹ جس کو دسعت دی گئی ہو۔</text></gloss>
</sense>
<sense id="8a7ff32a-28fd-4043-a6ee-9d3b527360c2" order="1">
<grammatical-info value="Adjective">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>fallacy of generalization</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>فلسفے یا منطق میں تعمیم کی غلطی</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>toorum ġeenḍaru uġarʰćayen, thaallo ġeenḍaru ġamuśaski bam. ho ġamuśaaski ses ġeenḍaru maneastemen. gute bar dincherum phaiṅ duwa. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Ten thieves were arrested, seven thieves were left-handed. It turns out, left-handed people are mostly thieves. This is fallacy of generalization. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
