<entry dateCreated="2020-07-27T07:12:49Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="doxná2_2190d2de-c6fc-4705-b62e-0c3874f3453f" guid="2190d2de-c6fc-4705-b62e-0c3874f3453f">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>doxná</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>BUR →  FA:  Smoke (دخن)</text></form>
</note>
<relation type="Compare" ref="ispandur_35a5fa98-28bf-4cb2-ab34-b83cf5272451"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>doxnʌ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>دوࣷخنہ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="3de714df-ee52-4ef2-95d5-0a8804380807">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>Like ancient Zoroastrians, Burusho people burn espand on ashes and embers to purify people and their living spaces of evil spirit with the smoke. The bed of ashes and embers where ispandur is sprinkled is called doxna.  </text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
