<entry dateCreated="2020-02-23T00:25:55Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="eća2_d028fd86-d963-4e06-93f1-5b696dd2d68e" guid="d028fd86-d963-4e06-93f1-5b696dd2d68e">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>eća</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>ɛtʃa</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>ایࣷچاࣷ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="5e89af4c-1830-410f-9864-3ced089e7398">
<gloss lang="en"><text>It is one of the speech dis-fluencies which means, 'that being said or so.'A word used as meaningless filler to introduce a new statement in addition to what was already stated</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>اُس کے بعد، کہنے یا کرنے کے بعد</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ne gali, eća, ja ne ġa bo sena bée. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>He went, that said, I did not say anything to him. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-10-16T00:34:10Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="eća1_36684415-c610-4179-bfec-b8a19665a3a1" guid="36684415-c610-4179-bfec-b8a19665a3a1">
