<entry dateCreated="2019-10-12T16:12:48Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="garum dan giraaśum_561ed1f6-3f47-4254-b9f9-bd4d287cb394" guid="561ed1f6-3f47-4254-b9f9-bd4d287cb394">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>garum dan giraaśum</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="phrase"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>garum dan giraːʃum</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>گرُم دن گراشُم</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="4b183e8c-cb80-412d-8f3c-759ac5db0835">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>hot stone play.  This outdoor game is played at nighttime. A white stone is warmed up and thrown away within a certain distance and participants are asked to fetch it. While it is darker outside the only visible stones are those which are white and the only way to find the right one is by touching the stones. Whoever brings the stone back (to the starting point) gets points. Finding the stone is relatively easier. The difficult part is getting the stone through the opposite team, whose members will come to snatch it by hook or by crook. Teammates are there to protect the stone finder. It is allowed to bring the stone stealthily. </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>یہ گیم رات کے اندھیر ے میں کھیلا جاتا ہے۔ایک سفید پتھر جو اندھیرے میں پہلے پھینک دیا جاتا ہے اور پھیر ڈھونڈ کر لانا ہوتا ہے۔ </text></gloss>
<trait name ="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.6.1 Game"/>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-11-05T15:29:44Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="garzenda_a28b95b1-d0a1-43a2-9d28-e5d19b259a78" guid="a28b95b1-d0a1-43a2-9d28-e5d19b259a78">
