<entry dateCreated="2019-09-19T04:31:45Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="ġainás_4b33454b-e278-47fe-bf2d-05ea5bad1c60" guid="4b33454b-e278-47fe-bf2d-05ea5bad1c60">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ġainás</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="ġotonás_0c229eab-072a-49a1-a586-03f084192fce"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>ɣainʌs</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>غینَس</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="f42904fa-76c2-4217-b12f-13fc490ee238">
<grammatical-info value="Adjective">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>Tandem-fed infant is called ġainás. In Burusho society, it is believed that breast-feeding babies are negatively affected by a pregnant mother. The taste and texture of the milk changes, and if the mother gives birth to a second child while the first one is still breastfeeding, he would be considered ġainas. The second child will be ġainas too if a 3rd one interrupts the breastfeeding period. </text></gloss>
<trait name ="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.2 Disease"/>
</sense>
</entry>
