<entry dateCreated="2019-09-11T04:46:15Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="ġolʰqos_505d1e5a-d938-48fb-8767-97f0ad5fb482" guid="505d1e5a-d938-48fb-8767-97f0ad5fb482">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ġolʰqos</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>ɣolʰqos</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>غوࣷلْقوࣷس</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Plural Suffix">
<form lang="bsk"><text>-s, śu</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="9ad1ab6d-0d91-4d43-96a6-288c04e6e8a0">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text> cistern. The ġolʰqós is a small underground pit or tank used to store drinking water. Its primary purpose is to keep the water clean and cool during the hot summer days. The tank is covered on all sides except for a small entrance. At the back of the tank, a water supply conduit connects to a nearby water channel. The tank is filled in the evening, allowing the water to cool down overnight, making it ready for consumption by the morning. During the day, the only source of cold water is from the ġolʰqós. This innovative water tank is operational only in the summertime and is believed to be a primitive water cooler utilized by the Burusho people.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>ٹانکھ، سردابہ، سرداب ،  زیر زمین پانی   کی ٹینکی۔</text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
