<entry dateCreated="2020-08-07T19:18:18Z" dateModified="2025-10-27T02:10:51Z" id="huṭaraṅ_5485283d-7aa8-430d-a489-e49c4532bc1f" guid="5485283d-7aa8-430d-a489-e49c4532bc1f">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>huṭaraṅ</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>Although the singular húṭ is no longer in active use, its plural form húṭiṅ (húṭ + iṅ) remains current in the language. The root húṭ shows notable phonological and semantic parallels with the English word foot, suggesting a possible ancient cognate or areal influence.</text></form>
</note>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>huʈaraŋ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>ہُٹرنٚ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Possessed">
<form lang="bsk"><text>huṭaraṅ</text></form>
</field>
<trait name="Possessors" value="U-Obligatorily Possessors"/>
<sense id="989ebfbd-9725-43f9-a256-a213b6d4f9d8">
<grammatical-info value="Adverb">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>Towards the feet side while lying down, foot-end of the bed. </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>پا ئینی، سونے کے حالت میں قدموں کی جانب</text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
