<entry dateCreated="2023-11-24T17:14:13Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="i1_8100de18-859e-402f-8815-c9056f304bbd" guid="8100de18-859e-402f-8815-c9056f304bbd">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>i</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<trait name="do-not-publish-in" value="Idioms"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>i</text></form>
</field>
<trait name="Past Participle" value="Past Participial"/>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>ئ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Possessed">
<form lang="bsk"><text>i</text></form>
</field>
<trait name="Possessors" value="DePrifix -i,u"/>
<sense id="5d1a4125-f8d2-4488-8a6b-ee83f30caf03">
<gloss lang="en"><text>In Burushaski, the verb "coming" in the past tense is constructed with the prefix /d-/ and /i/. Following /d-/, pertinent pronominal affixes are added, such as [da-, demi/e-, di-, du/o-, dumu/o-,  duku/o-], along with the /i/ infix and past tense suffixes.</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ja daiá.( d-a-i-a)</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>I came.</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>un dokoiá. (d-go-i-a)</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>You came. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ses duiá (d-u-i-á)</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>People came. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ja nani domoiá (d-mo-i-á)</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>My mother came.</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>alʰtan ses duién (d-u-i-en)</text></form>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>mi akholla demeiá (deme-i-á)</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>We came here.</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<trait name ="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9 Grammar"/>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2025-03-14T05:41:40Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="i2_17e6d935-a0e3-4c9e-b42c-787d93c9f5bb" guid="17e6d935-a0e3-4c9e-b42c-787d93c9f5bb">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>i</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<trait name="do-not-publish-in" value="Idioms"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>i</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>اِ/ یࣷ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="b686e38a-9909-48a1-828e-7195f3578194" order="0">
<gloss lang="en"><text>Pronominal Affix for 3SG.h.x. It is used as an infix, prefix and suffix in various inflectional forms of words.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>ضمیری لاحقہ یا سابقہ</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ne hire ikhar (i + khar) esqaní (esqan +í).</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>That man killed himself</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
<sense id="13ee7874-fa4e-4f68-8ae7-72d56ae89d84" order="1">
<gloss lang="en"><text>Verbal Suffix used for past, with 3SG.hm.x.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>لاحقہ جو فعل ماضی کے ساتھ لگتا ہے جہا فاعل مذکر (اسم ِایکس یا انسان ہو)</text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2021-03-28T05:03:16Z" dateModified="2023-11-10T16:01:13Z" id="-i_e510cd1c-33d5-474c-9296-a48cc3553122" guid="e510cd1c-33d5-474c-9296-a48cc3553122">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>-i</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="suffix"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="phátí_dbf8e292-4b1b-4147-8752-addd94389046"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>-i</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="42eceac7-7655-4ef1-8fb3-8525e9d15869">
<gloss lang="en"><text>with singular non-feminine subject, it forms past tense of verbs, provided the verb ends with consonants. </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>فعل حال کو ماضی میں تبدیل کردیتا ہے جہاں فاعل  واحد مذکر ہو بشتکہ مذکورہ فعل کی آواز vowel پہ ختم نہ ہو ۔ </text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ne gali.</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>He went. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ẓakune óṅ eti. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>The donkey brayed. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
