<entry dateCreated="2022-07-08T05:41:34Z" dateModified="2025-11-12T14:40:21Z" id="-ṣen_9e2c6604-cbe7-4de8-821e-959923f6b360" guid="9e2c6604-cbe7-4de8-821e-959923f6b360">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>-iṣen</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="suffix"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="-iṣ or ṣ_b802e5a6-7723-45b7-a488-1951a98cb470"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>-ʂɛn</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="c118a17e-d079-4ea6-a5ea-d7b757031730">
<gloss lang="en"><text>Post-nominal Modal suffix attached to verb, conveying sense of let them/those [verb], they may [verb]. It functions to expresses permission, approval, wishes or recommendation. It is used only with Plural verbs. With singular nouns, -iṣ is used. </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>کر لے، کریں یو جائے کے لیے استعمال ہوتا ہے۔یہ لاحقہ صرف جمع افعال کے ساتھ استعمال ہوتا ہے۔ واحد کے لیے –iṣ استعمال ہوتا ہے۔ </text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>we sese doro etiṣen. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Those people may/should work. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text><span lang="en">ma bariṅ chan maniṣ</span></text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>May your statements be true.  Your statement should be true. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
