<entry dateCreated="2022-10-20T02:50:51Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="kic̣i_d01e5ca6-4e3d-4794-82dc-9b2ebc7cd360" guid="d01e5ca6-4e3d-4794-82dc-9b2ebc7cd360">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>kic̣i</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>kiʈʂi</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>کِڅیࣷ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="cb638195-cc64-4038-a538-0af179123e61">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>A kíc̣i is a person who owns greater amount of family inheritance compare to his cousins due to the fact that he or his father has to share the inheritance with lessor number of siblings. If an inheritance is equally distributed between A and B, B is bound to be a kíc̣i if the number of B's children is lesser than that of A's.   </text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
