<entry dateCreated="2019-04-30T06:01:25Z" dateModified="2025-11-11T04:35:47Z" id="-kuc_f44cc332-d33d-4d40-9b9e-d5dbfcd88802" guid="f44cc332-d33d-4d40-9b9e-d5dbfcd88802">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>-kuc</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="suffix"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>It is probably a short form of gunz (day)</text></form>
</note>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>-kuts</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>کُڎ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="b5bd2719-6472-4403-b89b-dc646a2f49de">
<gloss lang="en"><text>The suffix -kuc attaches to numerals to express a time period in days, typically glossed as “for X days” or “X-day-long”.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text> اگڑ ہندوسوں کے ساتھ لگا دیا جائے تو دنوں کو بیا ن کرتا ہے۔ </text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>iskikuc (iski + kuc ), walʰṭkuc (walʰte + kuc)</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>three days, four days. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
