<entry dateCreated="2019-04-24T03:00:34Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="kurxat_312a573f-ceae-4ed9-8c73-d585d3e39344" guid="312a573f-ceae-4ed9-8c73-d585d3e39344">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>kurxat</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>In Yasin, it is believed that if you read some particular Quranic verses on a needle with coiled thread around it and place somewhere in the ceiling,  the missing animal will be protected overnight.  It has, however, become an archaic practice.</text></form>
</note>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>kurxat</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>کُرخت</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="d892fad7-ffda-49de-95d5-8c2a05418165">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>To protect missing animals against harm through occult practices or prayers</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>دم دعا  سے کھوئے ہو  ئے مال مویشی کے  گرد حفاظتی حصار ڈالنے کو کہتے ہیں۔ </text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
