<entry dateCreated="2019-03-22T04:20:05Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="lali_1c61c558-5a1a-4755-9605-79ae9a540d6e" guid="1c61c558-5a1a-4755-9605-79ae9a540d6e">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>láli</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text><span lang="bsk">It is more polite to use 'lali' when addressing a young man than the generic term halles which is more direct and less mannerly. However, it would not be considered rude when the term is being used from a position of authority. You do not want to call someone halles in any professional or formal setup.</span></text></form>
</note>
<relation type="Compare" ref="Kyaki_b7f62d5c-6bb3-4888-bf4b-d4ebe6b2c640"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>lʌli </text></form>
