</field>
<sense id="724adc0b-bd27-438e-9798-25cca1b69941">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>A galloping horse with short steps. laxwar is one of the several horse gates that the Burushaski speakers ascribe with horse. </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>گھوڑے کی  چال، ایسا گھوڑا جو  چھوٹے چھوٹے قدموں کے ساتھ انتہائی تیز  دوڑتا ہے۔</text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-05-01T19:39:01Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="le_ef49a1e0-7872-418c-ac86-fb2f7463cf48" guid="ef49a1e0-7872-418c-ac86-fb2f7463cf48">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>le</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>Though it is used only to address male (both SG and PL.), it is common to use it for both male and female where the understood majority is male.  </text></form>
</note>
<relation type="Compare" ref="doo_4ee2443a-ac55-43b2-b560-a65cedab3192"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>lɛ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>لےࣷ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="121389a2-63d1-4d1c-b4ec-87e3f07c03fb">
<grammatical-info value="Vocative (le, do)">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>hey, o </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>ارے(مردوں کے لیے ) </text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>le ac̣o</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>hey brother.</text></form>
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>ارے بھائی </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>le jaa tati. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>O, my father. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>le ses malʰtumall etiṅ. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>O, people, hear me out. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
