<entry dateCreated="2023-10-12T03:58:38Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="m_ff9dbf96-7941-4362-93bf-e1a26e4668ac" guid="ff9dbf96-7941-4362-93bf-e1a26e4668ac">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>m</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<trait name="do-not-publish-in" value="Idioms"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>m</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>م</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="0e146170-3d1c-42c8-9b10-9ccd5f6a8519">
<gloss lang="en"><text>It is used in Burushaski echo-words as a replacement of the first consonant of the second member. (Reduplication of the word) The eco-words give depreciative meaning to the original word. </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>بروشسکی کے مہمل الفاظ بنانے کے لیے استعمال ہوتا ہے جیسے اردو میں  "چائے وائے)</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ćai mai nume né. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Drink tea (or something) and go. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>gaṭunz maṭunz nuhalʰća cheran. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>After washing clothes (and all), we will go. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
