<entry dateCreated="2020-03-12T16:11:59Z" dateModified="2025-08-30T19:03:18Z" id="-naas_f4a9668c-6e50-4bb4-9692-b7183a6cfcd9" guid="f4a9668c-6e50-4bb4-9692-b7183a6cfcd9">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>-naas</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="suffix"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>The usage of this suffix as an agent noun is exclusive to the Burushaski of Yasin. It serves a different purpose in other  variants of Burushaski. </text></form>
</note>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>-naːs</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="a1d12f8d-4924-41e6-9256-365b2a8b4dca">
<grammatical-info value="V.">
<trait name="type" value="affix"/>
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>equivalent of English suffix "-er ", -nãs is used to create noun of agency or agent noun -- a person or thing that performs the action or the action is due upon the performer. </text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>Khene hir ajó girminaas ( girmin + naas) en bai. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>This man is a good writer. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>jaa ne echoġon ames heraas en bai. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>That little grandson of mine is a super weeper. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>khene girminaas jimell neaas bai. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>This writer is to go tomorrow.</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>girminaas jinari yaṭe bõ girminchum mayuum duwa. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>with a thing that writes, something is written (writing is done)</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
