<entry dateCreated="2023-07-07T00:08:06Z" dateModified="2025-11-06T16:37:30Z" id="nu_28a1b0ce-9557-48ce-b626-faa1a12a2516" guid="28a1b0ce-9557-48ce-b626-faa1a12a2516">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>nu</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>nu</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>نُو</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="cd52654c-6322-43c2-bbdd-69ae22f7d80c">
<gloss lang="en"><text>A converbial prefix used to express manner or after</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>دو افعال کے بیک وقت بیان کے لیے جیسے اردو میں رو کر، ہنس کر، دے کر وغیرہ</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ne nukuchar (nu + guchar) galí. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>He went by walking. (He could also go by running or by bus). </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ja aye nuher galí. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>My son went crying. (He was going- either the crying was done or he was still crying). </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<trait name ="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.5.1.4 Way, manner"/>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2021-01-08T17:50:10Z" dateModified="2025-11-06T16:18:56Z" id="nu -_8136c128-5666-49ef-924a-56e7b7b27a27" guid="8136c128-5666-49ef-924a-56e7b7b27a27">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>nu-</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="prefix"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>In non-causative converbial constructions of Burushaski, /nu/ functions as the default prefix, regardless of person or number. When causation is not involved, person and number distinctions are instead marked through vowel alternation or the insertion of pronominal infixes. Examples include: nu-guśiir, ni-śiir, nu-muśiir, na-śiir, na-maśiir. 

In the process of devoicing, certain word-initial consonants systematically shift to their voiceless counterparts:

- g (voiced velar stop) → k (voiceless velar stop) 
- b (voiced bilabial stop) → p (voiceless bilabial stop) 
- ġ (voiced uvular stop) → q (voiceless uvular stop)</text></form>
</note>
<relation type="Compare" ref="nuhu_102d8701-d153-4ef3-a1ec-e203618c552d"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="-ni_c6273cbc-9191-4d93-bc18-4f2691d43d1c"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="nukuyec_70bd3a43-a8e8-4b90-ac7a-c5b63df6452b"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>nu -</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>نُو</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="3c012a77-0dfa-40de-8800-ed4d2acc8ad4" order="0">
<gloss lang="en"><text>Converbial prefix that is used for 2,3PL to express 'after', where there is a causation involved.  </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>یہ سابقہ فعل کے ساتھ لگتا ہے اور بعد یا بعد از کا مفہوم  پیدا کرتا ہے۔</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>tiṣe peṭek nukuśiir (nu + guśiir) chućimi. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>The wind will take away your scarf, after snatching it from you. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ja ayuu Islamabad nuchú (nu + chu), phat oćam. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>I will leave my kids in Islmabad, after having taken them there. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
</example>
<example>
</example>
<example>
</example>
<example>
</example>
</sense>
<sense id="bf960c56-b5ec-4c18-9b1a-ffe529fa1158" order="1">
<gloss lang="en"><text>by way of, by </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>کر کے یا کے ذریعے </text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ne nukuchar gali</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>He went on foot (by walking) </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ne haġor yaṭe nuhulja gali. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>He went off by sitting astride on the horse. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
