<entry dateCreated="2021-01-10T02:29:42Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="nuú_cd07b530-81d1-4bfc-87c5-065a4e2a85ea" guid="cd07b530-81d1-4bfc-87c5-065a4e2a85ea">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>nuú</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text><span lang="bsk">Notice ni was used with țați (the father) and nu was used with yũ (his kids). Numo is used with güs (woman). With first person singular , na is used</span>.</text></form>
</note>
<relation type="Compare" ref="naa_f746bfdd-c84b-4b01-b315-6aaed8af4877"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>nuʊ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>نُوࣷ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="1afda824-fb21-4fbe-a79a-89d0f8b3a390">
<gloss lang="en"><text>(of animals and people) after (their) going</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>جانے کے بعد، جا کر۔یہ انسانوں اور جانوروں کے حوالے سے جمع کے لیے استعمال ہوتا ہے۔ </text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>yuu Giilʰt nuú, beérum dena, tati ka nī to huruṭi. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Several years after his kids went to Gilgit, the father went there too.</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
