<entry dateCreated="2021-11-27T02:11:25Z" dateModified="2025-11-11T16:52:00Z" id="-paći_3dd93f7c-9557-458a-8f4f-a62a619a1b77" guid="3dd93f7c-9557-458a-8f4f-a62a619a1b77">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>paći</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>A compound locative form expressing proximity or adjacency. Formed by contraction of the morpheme /pai/ (with, near) into pa, followed by the locative suffix -ći. 

Usage and interpretation vary by dialect: In Hunza, pa is a standalone noun meaning side, whereas in Yasin, pa functions as a locative or associative clitic, never used independently. Though with locative, ablative and dative case markers the word is commonly used in Yasin as well. Examples: apaći (a + pa + ći), near me, apaćum (a + pa +ćum) from near me or my side and apaća (a + pa +ća) to me or to my side. 

Here, paći is semantically equivalent to pai, both expressing nearness or accompaniment. 

Syntactic Note: - paći is always post-nominal—it follows the noun, with pronominal prefixes it modify. </text></form>
</note>
<relation type="Compare" ref="-pai_2e239307-302f-447d-9aa9-f01afb5ad0ce"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>-patʃi</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>بچی</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Possessed">
<form lang="bsk"><text>paći</text></form>
</field>
<trait name="Possessors" value="O-Obligatorily Possessors"/>
<sense id="7f530520-fe65-4f61-971e-a372291dd0be">
<grammatical-info value="Locative (ći, i)">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>near, beside, with, at the side of</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>ساتھ یا پاس</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>un jaa apaći hurúṭ</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>You sit near me. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ja apaći kheen apí. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>I do not have time (with me). </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
