<entry dateCreated="2020-04-19T18:16:46Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="patraanẓ_4d97a2b4-a2da-4dd0-af47-d103d8bcb6be" guid="4d97a2b4-a2da-4dd0-af47-d103d8bcb6be">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>patraanẓ</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>patraːnʐ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>پترنژ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Plural Suffix">
<form lang="bsk"><text>iṅ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="5a5583e0-c79a-47ad-9762-93297acb279c">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>The hunting face mask, traditionally crafted to resemble a fox, was primarily used during partridge hunting. Its design served both as camouflage and a cultural symbol, blending functionality with folklore.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>شکار ی کا ماسک جو مطلوبہ شکار کو دھوکہ دینے کے لیے استعمال ہوتا تھا۔  خاص کر چکور کے شکار کے لیے۔</text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
