<form lang="bsk"><text>miṅ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="b0a1302d-ddfd-4968-addf-1df271fb4d32" order="0">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>caress with hand</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>شفقت سے کسی کے سر پر ہاتھ پھیرنا۔ </text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>wawe jaġa phiri etu, da ja alʰćimo yaṭe báh etu </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Grandma caressed me and kissed on my eyes. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
<sense id="343faf1c-3ef3-4edd-a359-cecc1f266444" order="1">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>flying caress. waving one's hands in a circular motion from distance to express one's love. This is mostly observed among women in the Burusho society. </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>اظہار محبت میں اپنا ہاتھ ہوا میں کس کی طرف تواتر سے گھمانا۔ </text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
