<entry dateCreated="2022-01-20T22:47:26Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="phuwarenẓ_bcfba969-c88a-4cbd-a59a-d2a9dd311331" guid="bcfba969-c88a-4cbd-a59a-d2a9dd311331">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>phuwarenẓ</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="phü_0851d0f2-2a80-463d-a0b6-6e5e683341ed"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="wárenẓ_1eddcad4-1eff-468b-8d5b-ec492b5dbc96"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>pʰuwarɛnʐ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>پھُو برݩژ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Plural Suffix">
<form lang="bsk"><text>iṅ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="00195c2a-99b0-4d6e-8c39-ed50280706c1">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>A traditional method of long-distance communication used to convey warnings or messages. Personnel stationed at elevated vantage points—such as mountaintops—would signal the approach of enemies or imminent threats by producing visible smoke during daylight hours or igniting fires at night. These signals served as early warning systems in military or tribal contexts, enabling rapid response across vast terrains. </text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2020-06-02T19:58:15Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="phuẓaa_a8164274-0392-4951-9b1a-7a63ebd4f2a3" guid="a8164274-0392-4951-9b1a-7a63ebd4f2a3">
