<entry dateCreated="2020-08-15T21:07:00Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="qaqam máltaṣ_fefa635c-8ff6-4145-b516-43d3491af592" guid="fefa635c-8ff6-4145-b516-43d3491af592">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>qaqam máltaṣ</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="phrase"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>In Yásin, people traditionally package 2 to 5 kilograms of butter, wrap it in birch bark, and bury it in a water channel. The running water keeps the butter frozen in winter and cool in summer. This method of butter, in various forms, exists in different parts of the world such as bog butter in Europe. </text></form>
</note>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>qaqam mʌltaʂ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>ققم ملْتݜ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="5f845d35-1c12-48f0-8f73-40bcd42e03a9">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>aged butter (becomes bitter), bog butter</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>بُرانی کڑوی، دیسی گھی</text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
