<entry dateCreated="2019-10-23T15:21:23Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="rayát_8cba8d6d-c073-411f-abbb-05fcd6def846" guid="8cba8d6d-c073-411f-abbb-05fcd6def846">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>rayát</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>rayʌt</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>رئیات</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="532f5fb5-faca-4bf2-b524-d40e820efcd5">
<grammatical-info value="Adjective">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>(historic) people of different clans considered of lower class, primary because of the nature of their work  in society. They were tenant farmers or they worked for nobles or families of the so-called upper class including the  'thams'. Ryot, the Indian peasant is the closest sense of this term.  </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>یہ لوگ مختلف  قبیلوں سے تعلق رکھتے تھے لیکن اپنے کام  یا خدمت کی نوعیت کی وجہ سے کم ذات  یا خدمت گار تصور کئے جاتے تھے۔ </text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>khuwe ses rayat ses baan. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>These people are the rayat family. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-03-18T03:21:01Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="raǰün_f1f1e559-4ee0-40c0-a0c2-547d3b82483f" guid="f1f1e559-4ee0-40c0-a0c2-547d3b82483f">
