</field>
<trait name="Review 1" value="202509121"/>
<sense id="88450b57-dcd5-44de-81f5-8c239dafbf38">
<grammatical-info value="Postposition">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>Post-positional morpheme used with thape-gon (night) in the sense of 'throughout'</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>عموماً بھر کے معنوں میں رات کے ساتھ استعمال ہوتا ہے۔ </text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>thápe gónśar jaa dáṅ ayidiya. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>I could not sleep throughout the night. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2020-07-25T07:11:32Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="śár śár_4d74ce13-8d59-44d8-950f-9ffd160cba40" guid="4d74ce13-8d59-44d8-950f-9ffd160cba40">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>śár śár</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="phrase"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>ʃʌr ʃʌr</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>شرشر</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="2641bd9a-4265-4257-a523-d28932f63e6c">
<gloss lang="en"><text>melodious sound of rain or stream</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>رِم جِم، بارش یا پانی کی آواز</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>holle śar śar diyarʰci. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>It rained outside, with the melodious sound of rain. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>mo gus mo śar śar muu duuya. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Streams of tears flowed from her (eyes).</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
