<entry dateCreated="2019-10-26T15:37:07Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="śarbatau_56f22a37-7a10-45f9-87eb-211fabd65070" guid="56f22a37-7a10-45f9-87eb-211fabd65070">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>śarbatau</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="bát1_bba360da-3f45-4a35-a56c-1f0f36e25333"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>ʃarbatau</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>شربتاؤ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="3feafa5a-e1ea-43ee-853a-c7b893c181a0">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>A simple, uncooked condiment made by crushing fresh leaves of Himalayan barberry on a stone surface, typically with added salt. Commonly prepared by children outdoors as a casual activity; not considered a formal kitchen recipe.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>ایک قسم کی چٹنی جو بچے ہمالیائی بربری کے پتوں سے بناتے ہیں</text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2021-02-15T01:55:06Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="śareéġ_715ae4ec-33e4-43cd-a47c-a53cb0562490" guid="715ae4ec-33e4-43cd-a47c-a53cb0562490">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>śareéġ</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>

• A child born to parents of advanced age may be referred to as śareéġ, symbolizing late parenthood. 

• A fruit that ripens at the tail end of the harvest season, long after its counterparts, is also śareéġ.</text></form>
</note>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>ʃarɛɛɣ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>شریࣷغ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="a202960a-78b0-4d9f-9fc1-3ca394df4dd2">
<grammatical-info value="Adjective">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>A term describing a phenomenon or occurrence that takes place significantly later than the conventional or expected time. It conveys a sense of belatedness in relation to cultural, biological, or seasonal norms. </text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2020-06-02T16:30:06Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="śareki_d855ecb2-d444-4729-ac75-9a98ea99ef00" guid="d855ecb2-d444-4729-ac75-9a98ea99ef00">
