<entry dateCreated="2020-05-19T01:56:12Z" dateModified="2025-10-13T21:04:34Z" id="śiri_41269732-b3a9-449b-8a4e-370e8a5bad63" guid="41269732-b3a9-449b-8a4e-370e8a5bad63">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>śiri</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>ʃiri</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>شِری</text></form>
</field>
<trait name="Review 1" value="202510131"/>
<sense id="43aacb2d-f7dd-4905-8434-44f636957d79">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>A sacred term once used for a mythical entity—likely revered or worshiped by the Burushos—is now extinct. However, a central pillar in the upper portion of a traditional Burusho house is still called śirii duṅ (“the pillar of śiri”).</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>ایک دیوی کا نام جسے کسی زمانے میں پوجھا جاتا تھا۔ </text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2025-08-23T19:06:01Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="śiri duṅ_bd56384a-52ee-41b8-b621-672ae5278fdd" guid="bd56384a-52ee-41b8-b621-672ae5278fdd">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>śiri duṅ</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="phrase"/>
<relation type="_component-lexeme" ref="">
<trait  name="complex-form-type" value="Unspecified Complex Form"/>
</relation>
<trait name="do-not-publish-in" value="Idioms"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>ʃiri duŋ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>شری دُنٚ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="6a482b74-ebc2-44d5-9db9-8461ee07a878">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>In a traditional Burusho house, the central pillar among the three smaller pillars in the upper area is known as śiri duṅ. This pillar is considered sacred and holds significant spiritual importance. As part of traditional rituals, a portion of consecrated or symbolic food—such as milk or butter oil—is first offered to the śiri duṅ before being distributed to others. This act reflects reverence for ancestral spirits and the sanctity of the home.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>گھر کے بالائی حصے میں مرکرزی ستون جس کو مقدس درجہ حاصل ہے۔ </text></gloss>
<trait name ="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.5.1 Building"/>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2020-08-16T06:16:26Z" dateModified="2025-10-13T21:12:52Z" id="śirini_c5394ba4-58a9-4f33-b9ba-c2d243e3c4ff" guid="c5394ba4-58a9-4f33-b9ba-c2d243e3c4ff">
