<entry dateCreated="2022-11-19T15:14:59Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="śiti_5a431b91-f8c5-40cd-a300-6b1ad63e18e6" guid="5a431b91-f8c5-40cd-a300-6b1ad63e18e6">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>śiti</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="bend2_7c62d3d3-8ec7-457d-af3c-23e22c71c650"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>ʃiti</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>شِتی</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="381971ae-c527-40db-ae4d-57ac7fc67a49">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>In a traditional Burusho house, the area around the hearth where people sit is called śiti. Historically, this space lacked wood flooring or carpeting. The concept of śiti is closely associated with tik (soil); once wood flooring is installed, the area is referred to as bend.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>ریوایتی گھر میں آگ کے آس پاس والی جگہ جہا ں بیٹھتے ہیں شِتی کہا جاتا ہے۔ </text></gloss>
<trait name ="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.5.1 Building"/>
</sense>
</entry>
