<sense id="afa63176-123d-4a9a-b91a-96701f4883f5">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>Court dignitaries — Individuals who are in some way affiliated with the royal court. These may include nobles, advisors, officials, or esteemed figures who hold influence or perform duties within the royal establishment</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>درباری اکابرین۔ ایسے لوگ جو شاہی دربار میں کسی نہ کسی طرح منسلک ہوں۔</text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-10-21T01:28:59Z" dateModified="2025-09-17T03:32:42Z" id="ṣadari_f5d58313-3091-402f-84ff-3022629992db" guid="f5d58313-3091-402f-84ff-3022629992db">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ṣadari</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>ʂadari</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Plural Suffix">
<form lang="bsk"><text>-r, ṅ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="d7c06002-7fa0-458c-9b18-5df6baa35bc1">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>ṣadari is a royal convocation where all the tribal chiefs, notables and influential people gather in the royal court or the royal fort to ensure attendance, to pay respect to the king and to participate in decisions pertaining to critical state affairs. Essentially, it was this system through which rule of a lawless country was possible. </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>ݜدر کا  منصب</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ṣadar haalle baya?</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Is the chief (available) at home? </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
