<entry dateCreated="2019-09-24T14:52:41Z" dateModified="2025-09-20T16:49:41Z" id="ṣit1_3078caf3-24fe-46d8-b22c-e573b386557a" guid="3078caf3-24fe-46d8-b22c-e573b386557a">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ṣit</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>ʂit</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="30debe25-5af7-459d-b93c-616dd32e1dda">
<gloss lang="en"><text>(of two bodies or joints) so fit against each other that there is no gap in between. </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>دو چیزوں کاایک دوسرے کے ساتھ ایسا جوڑ جانا کہ ان کی بیچ میں کوئی جگہ باقی نہ رہے۔ </text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>hiṅ ṣiṭ et. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Make the door gap-free (Close it fully)</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>dapiski nukudell, ball ce ṣit goćam. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>I will flatten you against the wall, after having you kicked. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
