<sense id="d0db0787-96e2-46aa-b7cc-3d9253b9e55e" order="0">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>A ceremonial food portion sent by the groom to a married woman by the groom who is either related to him or hails from his village or tribe. This gesture serves as a heartfelt reminder that even though she has left her natal home, she remains cherished and remembered during moments of joy and sorrow. It’s a symbolic act of inclusion, kinship, and emotional continuity </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>سو غات </text></gloss>
</sense>
