<entry dateCreated="2020-05-11T22:16:31Z" dateModified="2025-11-05T04:36:09Z" id="tamusi_43b6dca9-df49-4ff0-8229-7d1090fd2813" guid="43b6dca9-df49-4ff0-8229-7d1090fd2813">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>tamusi</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="istau_06653aa4-0509-4a4a-aeb2-e945e3acdb18"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="mayen1_014d84a9-ba00-4d8c-8083-f46fe7bd2539"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>tamusi</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>تمُسی</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="f4714e4a-affe-4880-9e1b-447bbaa9901d">
<grammatical-info value="Adjective">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>fallow, tamusi refers to a fallow field—land that is plowed and harrowed but left unsown to restore fertility and vigor.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>غیر کا شت شدہ کھیت جس پر ہل چلا کر بغیربیج بو کر چھوڑ دیا جاتا ہے تاکہ مٹی کی زرخیزی بحال ہو۔ اُردو زبان میں اسے رُلا کہا جاتا ہے۔   </text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>gute máll akhoći ayharićan, gute tamusi phatćan (phat ećam)</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>This year, let's not plow this field, let's leave it as fallow. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-08-26T17:18:14Z" dateModified="2025-11-05T04:37:30Z" id="tan2_f19bbe5a-fdcb-479c-a67d-16de3e6fe598" guid="f19bbe5a-fdcb-479c-a67d-16de3e6fe598">
