<sense id="75c7a6f0-4023-43cf-9a69-c8ec4df137bb">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>summer sojourn, upland pasture,  highland settlement where people live in summer  </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>پہاڑی علاقوں میں بالائی علاقہ جہاں گرمیوں میں لوگ رہتے ہیں۔ </text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2020-07-20T21:36:44Z" dateModified="2025-11-07T19:54:42Z" id="tera mál ġare oćum_f6ab9fb1-497d-4687-b214-141e78c4e61e" guid="f6ab9fb1-497d-4687-b214-141e78c4e61e">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>tera mál ġare oćumj </text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>tɛra mʌl ɣarɛ otʃum</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>تیࣷرا مل غرےࣷ اوࣷچُم</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="bcb1c9f9-c62a-4483-81d8-4b22b646510d">
<grammatical-info value="Verb">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>Asking a neighbor or anybody – who is willing – to take one's flock of animals for a pastoral stay in the highland summer pasture is a custom. The agreeing party would mix the animals with his own's and will take care of them the whole summer season. He will shepherd them, guard them, and return them to the owner— often with some butter and other dairy products, proportionally set aside. This seasonal arrangement of  villagers is called  țéra mál gharé ochüm  . Such arrangement is often between relatives but could be for a remuneration as well. One form of remuneration is gyén that is provided to the agreeing party.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>اپنے مال مویشوں کو  کسی دوسرے کے حوالے کرنا تاکہ وہ گرمیوں کے موسم میں اپنے مویشیوں کے ساتھ ملا کر اُن کی رکھوالی کریں اور گرمیوں کے بعد واپس کریں۔  </text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>akhoći ja mal ġare otam ba, aya tera ay neyam ba.</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>I, myself, have not gone to the ter this year. My cattle are mixed with (someone else' cattle). </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
