<entry dateCreated="2019-09-23T17:30:52Z" dateModified="2025-11-07T21:54:32Z" id="thás2_8cd87d04-2d9b-4b1a-ab2c-b165fd4fbccc" guid="8cd87d04-2d9b-4b1a-ab2c-b165fd4fbccc" order="2">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>thás</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>thʌs</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>تھس</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="6021327e-93f9-4032-a50b-5e5de67b4104">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>A term used as a unit for counting households likely originates from the Burushaski word thas, meaning the smoke rising from a traditional home. In this context, visible smoke from a chimney indicates that the house is inhabited and active, and thus qualifies to be counted as a household</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>آبادی  کو گننے کے لیے استعمال ہوتا ہے۔گھرانا </text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>Sandi beerum thás ses baan?</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>How many households of people are there in Sandi Village?</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
