<entry dateCreated="2022-11-13T20:26:09Z" dateModified="2025-11-10T02:37:02Z" id="tiliki_aa0e3b5e-6994-4472-ae5b-6e94248c6174" guid="aa0e3b5e-6994-4472-ae5b-6e94248c6174">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>tiliki</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>tiliki</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>تِلِکی</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="757e9838-550a-4abb-a5f5-a9b53d8a5a9f">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>In the the agrarian Burusho culture, spreading fertilizer—particularly manure—is a labor-intensive task typically carried out with the help of neighbors or volunteers. As a gesture of gratitude, the host family prepares a special bread called tiliki for those who assist.</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>delʰk giyen ka tiliki mi ġa bim. </text></form>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2022-10-25T04:54:10Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="tiliseri_7408faf1-13bc-43fa-a90a-be60c8016205" guid="7408faf1-13bc-43fa-a90a-be60c8016205">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>tiliseri</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
