<relation type="Compare" ref="ambóh_5c1ed0a5-c3de-4e54-ab92-da594e5a656d"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>tilisum</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>تِلِسُم </text></form>
</field>
<sense id="ded3f3f4-acfd-49ec-95f0-3c2569436c17">
<gloss lang="en"><text>myriad, extremely large number</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>ہزار ہا، لاتعداد یا بے شمار</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>tilisum ses gati manen</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Myriad of people got together. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2022-11-05T14:50:47Z" dateModified="2025-11-08T03:15:11Z" id="till_07a85eaa-49c9-4130-b050-fbe6bd64ed0c" guid="07a85eaa-49c9-4130-b050-fbe6bd64ed0c">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>till</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="táp3_d0301c96-27db-46e0-a8fb-292f9f3429f4"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>tiɫ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>تلٚ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="e038004d-9e6f-447e-a498-83dc172fd41d">
<gloss lang="en"><text>The verb infix /-ll-/ is obligatorily used and requires inflectional affixes for both tense and person. In the causative mood, this bound morpheme changes to /-skil-/. For example, “make him forget” is expressed as: ne till eeskil. till itself has no meaning. </text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2021-02-22T00:18:50Z" dateModified="2025-11-08T03:21:59Z" id="till aalla_29801516-c278-4c19-b9e1-1985044fac5c" guid="29801516-c278-4c19-b9e1-1985044fac5c">
<lexical-unit>
