<form lang="bsk"><text>tiɫ amaːliŋ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="b5f44a26-67ba-4662-901e-7149099ce2f2">
<grammatical-info value="Imperative Plural">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>Do not forget (When speaking  to more  than one person)</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>مت بھولو ( جمع متکلم)</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ja te doro etiṅ, till amaliṅ</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Do that work of mine, do not forget. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-04-24T15:06:34Z" dateModified="2025-11-08T03:09:52Z" id="till golʰćum_3c96276c-340a-4337-b8f7-4721148e4828" guid="3c96276c-340a-4337-b8f7-4721148e4828">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>till golʰćum</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="phrase"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>The word till is always used with the bound morpheme -ll-, which takes pronominal prefixes and inflectional suffixes. In the example alla, there are three morphemes: a (1SG prefix), -ll- (bound root morpheme), and the final -a (past tense suffix for 1SG). Similarly, the word golʰćum consists of three morphemes: go (2SG prefix), -ll- (bound morpheme), and -ćum (a suffix that forms a gerund).</text></form>
</note>
<relation type="Compare" ref="goski ddokoshüm_f7a5869a-de9c-4404-9151-24b100780cb1"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>tiɫ golʰtʃum</text></form>
</field>
<trait name="Past Participle" value="Past Participial"/>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>تِلٚ گوࣷلْچُم</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Possessed">
<form lang="bsk"><text>ll</text></form>
</field>
<trait name="Possessors" value="O-Obligatorily Possessors"/>
<sense id="48351b2c-c9b9-4a69-9691-61c7f5313e08">
<grammatical-info value="Verb/Verbal Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>forgetting</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>بھول جانا</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ja till alla (a-ll-a)</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>I forgot.</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>un till goolla. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>You forgot. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>we till ollen. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>They forgot. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
