<form lang="bsk"><text>tis</text></form>
</field>
<trait name="Noun Class" value="Bi "/>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>تِس</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Plural Suffix">
<form lang="bsk"><text>-s, śanz</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="d8149aaf-6881-4829-a5a5-55fee46580f3">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>This is a grain storage pit. In Yasin, where the land is dry, cylindrical pits are used to store grain. The opening of each pit is sealed with stone slabs, birch bark (hali), and a heap of earth. These underground grain pits are located at a distance from dwellings—a strategic measure to ensure continued access to essential food supplies during wartime looting or siege by foreign attackers.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>اگندم کو زمین کے اندر رکھنے کا گڑھا </text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>phallo tiśa gí. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Put the grain in the tis. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>tiśum phallo diyaśa. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Take out the grain from the storage pit. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-09-19T15:31:12Z" dateModified="2025-11-08T02:08:47Z" id="tiśi_ac915cbf-307a-49d9-ab61-ef3c1bc81182" guid="ac915cbf-307a-49d9-ab61-ef3c1bc81182">
