<entry dateCreated="2019-09-29T16:05:50Z" dateModified="2025-11-08T00:35:07Z" id="tota_0e9b184b-5f02-492c-a975-3f49978d55a1" guid="0e9b184b-5f02-492c-a975-3f49978d55a1">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>toota</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>  </text></form>
</note>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>tota</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>توتاࣷ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="486a96fa-9557-4995-8985-a827ab2316d6">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>A practice or play where adults hold a baby's hand and encourage to toddle. This is done with an ancient toddling song that reads as:
toota ka tota,
baliṅe khaći toota.
ćhumare daroġo
toota. girʰkise
baya, toota.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>بچے کا ہاتھ پکڑکر  گیت گاکرپہلی بار  چلنا سکھانے کا عمل۔</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>lali toota et.</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Walk the toddler.</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
