<entry dateCreated="2022-10-25T21:33:55Z" dateModified="2025-11-03T00:41:12Z" id="tuli wáśćum_9f4af210-d2fe-45e7-966e-a8750abca63b" guid="9f4af210-d2fe-45e7-966e-a8750abca63b">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>tuli wáśćum</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="phrase"/>
<relation type="_component-lexeme" ref="">
<trait  name="complex-form-type" value="Phrasal Verb"/>
</relation>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>tuli wʌʃtʃum</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>تُلی وشچُم</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="df5d4163-2ef9-41b5-bd4f-9db702078779">
<grammatical-info value="Verb/Verbal Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>A toss is conducted, with team captains selecting between two options—such as heads or tails, sun or moon. The winner of the toss earns the right to make a key decision, such as choosing which side to start on. This is called tuli waśćum. </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>ٹاس کرنا</text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
