<entry dateCreated="2022-10-24T14:08:49Z" dateModified="2025-11-08T03:42:43Z" id="tuuli_9170facd-ebd0-4009-9ed1-e454979fb637" guid="9170facd-ebd0-4009-9ed1-e454979fb637">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>tuuli</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="tuleéni_16639716-d9b4-4f8e-86ca-3a0723073edf"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>tuːli</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>تُولِی</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="f3bcd470-ee5d-4600-945b-5e0174e109fc">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>Anything that has a peg-like or pin-shaped form may be referred to as tuuli. This term applies broadly to pointed or upright objects. For example, a mountain peak may be called tuuli, while a small, slender item such as a matchstick may be referred to as tuuli.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>جو چیز بھی میخ یا کیل جیسی شکل رکھتی ہو، اسے تولی کہا جا سکتا ہے۔ یہ لفظ نوکیلی یا سیدھی کھڑی اشیاء کے لیے استعمال ہوتا ہے۔</text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2021-01-20T16:53:31Z" dateModified="2025-10-31T14:56:12Z" id="ṭaak2_a864e429-79ff-4c37-a386-ad0a5c30ff13" guid="a864e429-79ff-4c37-a386-ad0a5c30ff13">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ṭaak</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>ʈaːk</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>ٹاک</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="4e82c29d-1e16-4265-b391-cf9af5ab3334">
<grammatical-info value="Adjective">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>tenuous, fragile condition, especially used in the sense of minimal cohesion</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>نازک یا کمزور مگر ٹھیک (جیسے سلائی کا جوڑنا ، صحت یابی وغیرہ) </text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>jaa gaṭunz ṭaak ót</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Tack my clothes together. (Here the word stitching is downplayed to evoke fragility). </text></form>
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>ا</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ja lahaz bám, amutuk phuk an ṭaak amanam ba. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>I was unwell. I am better now, though only barely.</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-10-05T15:45:34Z" dateModified="2025-10-31T15:25:20Z" id="ṭaak1_42b24de6-bc5b-420a-9b55-dbfb829f9c6b" guid="42b24de6-bc5b-420a-9b55-dbfb829f9c6b">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ṭaak</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>ʈaːk</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>ٹاک</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="bf9ddc4f-7737-445f-ab0a-c7f36919c748">
<grammatical-info value="Adjective">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>not fully recovered, just on the recovery path, tenuously ok. </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>ابھی مکمل  صحت یاب نہ ہو۔</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>I was unwell. I’m better now, though only barely.</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>I have recovered a bit, I am not well as yet.</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-05-20T00:35:49Z" dateModified="2025-10-31T15:29:41Z" id="ṭaak ećum1_c766d3c6-cd31-471f-b069-cd293113221e" guid="c766d3c6-cd31-471f-b069-cd293113221e">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ṭaak ećum</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="phrase"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>ʈaːk ɛtʃum</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>ٹاک ایࣷچُم</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="0ced2c73-ae4a-4aa9-9c80-f136aefb99a4">
<grammatical-info value="Verb/Verbal Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>tentatively tying something with</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>کسی جانور کو عارضی طور پر باندھنا</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>haġor terek ce ṭaak et. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Tie the horse with the poplar tree for a bit. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-05-20T00:39:37Z" dateModified="2025-10-31T15:52:33Z" id="ṭaak ećum2_76e0193d-9204-43c9-b8e8-9030241da48b" guid="76e0193d-9204-43c9-b8e8-9030241da48b">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ṭaak ećum</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="phrase"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>ʈaːk ɛtʃum</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>ٹاک ایࣷچُم</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="3a23c808-794c-4965-b4b6-03bc4138bdb9">
<grammatical-info value="Verb/Verbal Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>(of construction) building something that you can temporarily live in, provisional arrangement, putting together. </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>تعمیر  جس میں گزارا کیا جاسکے جب تک مکمل گھر تعمیر نہیں ہوتا</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>koṭaránṭaak net ṭawulle huruśan</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>We will build a room and live in there. (until something else is arranged)</text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2020-03-12T15:45:52Z" dateModified="2025-11-02T03:09:18Z" id="ṭaanjo_bf5d7794-9071-4126-8d77-70e69611fc53" guid="bf5d7794-9071-4126-8d77-70e69611fc53">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ṭaanjo</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
