<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>جھاڑ، جھڑکا دے کر  کسی چیز کو گرانا، خالی کرنا </text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>gatunz ṭhak ót. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Shake off the clothes. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-12-22T18:25:53Z" dateModified="2025-10-08T01:12:46Z" id="ṭhák3_12dbc0ca-2cd3-424f-ab09-59934002aec6" guid="12dbc0ca-2cd3-424f-ab09-59934002aec6">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ṭhák</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>ʈhʌk</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>ٹھک</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="0816bc92-4af2-4116-a155-2ba6c60dc39f">
<grammatical-info value="Adjective">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>rattled out and empty, shook off and empty</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>کسی چیز سے خالی  یا چھٹکارا،خاص کرجھڑکا دینے کے بعد  </text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>gumemo ṭhak gooćam.</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>I will make your teeth rattled out and empty. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-05-13T18:06:01Z" dateModified="2025-11-06T20:22:58Z" id="ṭhampóq_d694ac92-cffa-4a8e-b15c-eb192ec40ecc" guid="d694ac92-cffa-4a8e-b15c-eb192ec40ecc">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>ṭhampóq</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>In Balti it is called da-phok.</text></form>
</note>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>ʈhampɔq</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>ٹھمپوࣷق</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Plural Suffix">
<form lang="bsk"><text>iśu</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="3cfd86fc-f5b2-4dad-b39a-c94fd36d27e2">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>In polo, teams switch ends after each goal is scored. Following a goal, the scorer gallops toward the opposing team’s goalpost, holding both the ball and mallet in one hand. Upon reaching the center of the field, he tosses the ball into the air and strikes it with full force. This dramatic, high-speed strike is known as ṭhampóq  </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>پولو  میں  گیند کو ہوا  میں  چھوڑنا اور پھر مارنا</text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
