<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>This wooden billet (thük) is about 4 inch. Both side of the billet are diagnally cut to make it look like shurr (spout) so that it is easy to tap it on one side with the stick and hit it in the air. For that reason, it is also called thükŝhüri</text></form>
</note>
