<entry dateCreated="2019-05-20T14:19:57Z" dateModified="2025-10-22T22:44:40Z" id="waqe panji_06d5d801-8144-415b-869a-9ac4e74d4e43" guid="06d5d801-8144-415b-869a-9ac4e74d4e43">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>waqe panji</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="phrase"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>waqɛ panʒi</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>وقےࣷ پنجی</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="d2baa245-642f-4414-9b3d-89dc98a1d0b7">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>A cairn placed by a team that showed up for a contest where the other team didn’t. It marks the presence and readiness of one side, and the absence of the other.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>جیت اور بہادری کی نشانی جو پتھر وں  کو ایک دوسرے کے اوپر رکھ کر بنا یا جاتا ہے۔ </text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>wee waq ooti, ẓoiṅ waqe panji ećan.</text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>Their (ass) became wide open (of fear), let's make the cairn of cowards. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
<illustration href="panji.PNG">
<label>
<form lang="bsk"><text>panji</text></form>
</label>
</illustration></sense>
</entry>
