<entry dateCreated="2019-08-27T20:55:02Z" dateModified="2025-10-23T01:25:33Z" id="xada_24db5d5a-c28f-4117-93d4-26b7055597b6" guid="24db5d5a-c28f-4117-93d4-26b7055597b6">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>xada</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text> ġada in Tibetan means a mace or club, possibly a loan word from Buruśaaski. </text></form>
</note>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>xada</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>خدہ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="494db790-f7e2-4719-8792-81b577541b21" order="0">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>A long wooden pole used to strike and dislodge fruit from trees like walnut and apricot.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>پھل  وغیرہ  گرانے کے لیے استعمال ہونے والا  لمبا سا ڈنڈا</text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>xada yaṭe telle duguc̣umaan</text></form>
<translation>
<form lang="en"><text><span lang="bsk">xada (a long wooden pole) is used to strike down walnut.</span></text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
<sense id="305bf95d-7dc2-4b58-ad99-52d561833158" order="1">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>A long wooden pole, with a loop at one end, used to catch falcons at night. </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>ایک لمبا سا ڈنڈا  جس کے ایک سرے پر گھوڑے کی دم کے بال کا پھندہ ہوتا ہے  جو رات کو باز پکڑنے کے لیے استعمال ہوتا ہے۔ </text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-03-27T04:19:21Z" dateModified="2025-10-23T01:26:48Z" id="ǩhai_fd55b12a-7196-4b4e-93f6-8a1f4c1fa251" guid="fd55b12a-7196-4b4e-93f6-8a1f4c1fa251">
