<entry dateCreated="2019-10-23T15:31:18Z" dateModified="2025-10-23T03:03:42Z" id="xanazat_eb917bbd-6f88-47a9-a319-0261fa7f482a" guid="eb917bbd-6f88-47a9-a319-0261fa7f482a">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>xanazat</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>xanazat</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>خناࣷزَت</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="04e63f62-f46a-4ed7-a38c-6b31cf09831f">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>(history) person or persons bound to be at the service of someone else. Historically they were the people lived and worked on the ruler's estate. They were entirely depended on the keeper for their subsistence. Anybody could become xanazat for reasons beyond one's control.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>خانہ ذات، وہ جو  کسی راجہ یا چودھری کے گھر پر کام کر کے  زندگی کو چلائے۔</text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2020-05-23T03:44:30Z" dateModified="2025-10-23T03:04:24Z" id="xanazati_c559ed7c-59f0-4fe0-a037-89d5aca3820c" guid="c559ed7c-59f0-4fe0-a037-89d5aca3820c">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>xanazati</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>xanazati</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>خنزَتیࣷ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="caf28c3e-864f-4fa0-935a-e327e605485a">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>bondage, being in the state of xanazat</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>کسی کے ہاں خدمت پر مامور  ہونا یا غلامی کرنا۔  </text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-10-15T18:40:52Z" dateModified="2025-10-23T21:07:57Z" id="xanjo_b337ba06-c60e-494f-af45-d1dccab58035" guid="b337ba06-c60e-494f-af45-d1dccab58035">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>xanjo</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="bexanjo_3ea5a139-8ed0-4e81-83a9-42d850d2dfdd"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>xanʒo</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>خنجوࣷ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="0753e447-b4ed-4845-816c-d22ce6488e2e">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>mixing a little flour with spices to sauté something is called xanjo</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>تھوڑے سے آٹا  ملا کر  سالن کے لیے مسالا</text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2020-05-25T05:59:21Z" dateModified="2025-10-23T21:05:15Z" id="xaṅgi_14374aa4-7e35-473f-be1f-8f4a007aac6e" guid="14374aa4-7e35-473f-be1f-8f4a007aac6e">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>xaṅgi</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="boin_71a46b40-e5ca-4c07-b283-2ecc6e8ff02b"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>xaŋgi</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>خنٚگیࣷ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Plural Suffix">
<form lang="bsk"><text>mo</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="a7952b5f-5219-4005-832b-9fd41d338566" order="0">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>The xaṅgi is a household goddess believed to safeguard the home. When a snake appears inside the house, it is regarded not as an ordinary creature, but as a loyal manifestation of the xaṅgi. Elders—especially octogenarians—insist the snake must not be harmed, and it is respectfully allowed to leave on its own. The snake itself is not the goddess; rather, it is believed that the xaṅgi takes the form of a snake to visit and protect the household.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>دیومالائی تصور جس میں خنگی  دیوی سانپ کی شکل میں گھر یا گھر  کی چاردیواری کی حفاظت کرتا ہے۔ سانپ اگر گھر کے اندر نظرآ جائے تو اُسے نقصان نہیں پہنچایاجاتا۔ </text></gloss>
</sense>
<sense id="918ee296-f16f-49c0-b20f-ad5c005c74b6" order="1">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>(fig) a person very attached to someone, mostly used for young children. </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>وہ جو کسی کے ساتھ زیادہ مانوس ہو خاص کر چھوٹا بچہ </text></gloss>
<example>
<form lang="bsk"><text>khene ames ho ja xaṅgi bai, ana galla ka akaaṭ rahi bai. </text></form>
<translation type="Free translation">
<form lang="en"><text>This grandchild of mine is very attached to me, he is ready to go with me wherever I go. </text></form>
</translation>
</example>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2024-07-14T16:59:08Z" dateModified="2025-12-26T17:08:31Z" id="xáp3_08894f2b-bbdb-4a65-8cf8-97da0d9c5ba2" guid="08894f2b-bbdb-4a65-8cf8-97da0d9c5ba2" order="1">
