<entry dateCreated="2019-10-15T16:14:26Z" dateModified="2025-10-23T23:07:37Z" id="xaarʰćiki_2e645147-79f1-45b8-b94b-987453ced62a" guid="2e645147-79f1-45b8-b94b-987453ced62a">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>xarʰćiki</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="xarʰc_34f43b1c-e677-4b16-9cf1-105c4281fc5f"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>xaːr̥tʃiki</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>خرْچِکیࣷ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="87e58bb0-38ca-4c86-b148-eaba794f98ec">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>Xarʰćiki is a pre-wedding tradition observed the day before the main ceremony. Close relatives and neighbors gather at each family's home to celebrate, entertain guests, and finalize preparations. Both sides hold their own xãřchiki, marking joyful anticipation and communal support for the upcoming wedding.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>شادی کے دن سے ایک دن پہلے خرْچِکیࣷ کی رسم منائی جاتی ہے یہ مہندی کی طرح کا ایک رسم ہوتا ہے۔  </text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
