<entry dateCreated="2019-09-17T04:19:54Z" dateModified="2025-10-28T14:14:46Z" id="yaráq_2a089f6b-873f-46af-ae35-5c2e608dbdd5" guid="2a089f6b-873f-46af-ae35-5c2e608dbdd5">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>yaráq</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>yarʌq</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>یرَق</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="bfae8670-93c5-4916-8a8e-1629932f60cb">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>The process of cooling down a horse, after a journey, race or polo match. In this process the horse is tied up so that it does not eat or drink until it is cooled down. Once the horse is cooled down, food and water can be given. This practice is calle yaráq in Burushaski. This practice is essential to save the horse from complicaiton such as heat stress and colic. </text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>ریس یا سفر کے بعد  گھوڑے کو (کھانے اور پانی نہ دے کر  باندھنا تاکہ اُس کا جسم ٹھنڈا ہو جائے اور مخلیف پیچدگیوں سے بچ جائے۔ </text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2019-04-15T03:14:14Z" dateModified="2025-10-29T01:50:06Z" id="yárrayum_24d3ffd6-a2fa-4065-99ff-45291e247ebd" guid="24d3ffd6-a2fa-4065-99ff-45291e247ebd">
