<entry dateCreated="2020-05-12T01:45:41Z" dateModified="2025-10-28T14:23:26Z" id="yargá_59b91e6e-f1f3-4691-8943-d8c5005c7173" guid="59b91e6e-f1f3-4691-8943-d8c5005c7173">
<lexical-unit>
<form lang="bsk"><text>yargá</text></form>
</lexical-unit>
<trait  name="morph-type" value="stem"/>
<note>
<form lang="en"><text>Please see entries under yar and gu as etymological reference to this practice. </text></form>
</note>
<relation type="Compare" ref="yarguc̣um_68f1416f-e617-4a7e-937d-e500a0aacb3e"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="gu3_49df2f16-582f-4958-85ab-c1b46e9396e3"/>
<relation type="Compare" ref="yár1_ef95970b-2be3-4864-b7dc-87b1a08f8b21"/>
<field type="IPA Burushaski">
<form lang="bsk"><text>yargʌ</text></form>
</field>
<field type="Perso Arabic Burushaski">
<form lang="ur-PK"><text>یرگہ</text></form>
</field>
<sense id="8512cc2a-04ca-477e-87c8-f980f200462c">
<grammatical-info value="Noun">
</grammatical-info>
<gloss lang="en"><text>Battue hunting. A hunting technique in which villagers would mobilize across vast areas of mountain or jungle to corner game into a specified area. This practice was usually to help rulers hunt game. This practice was known as 'nerge' or 'jarga' in the Mongol Empire. The Buruśo also used this technique to chase down a wolf hidden in riverside bushes.</text></gloss>
<gloss lang="ur-PK"><text>شکا ر کا ایک طریقہ جس میں ایک گروہ پہاڑ کے ایک بڑے حصے پر یا جنگل کا گراؤ کرکے شکار کرتا ہے۔ ہنکان </text></gloss>
</sense>
</entry>
<entry dateCreated="2021-02-21T05:26:22Z" dateModified="2025-10-28T14:28:19Z" id="yarguc̣um_68f1416f-e617-4a7e-937d-e500a0aacb3e" guid="68f1416f-e617-4a7e-937d-e500a0aacb3e">
<lexical-unit>
